+# CD menu and startup update - 2026-10-02
+
+Default Pi: 192.168.1.19, user volumio, source /home/volumio/sable.
+
+Measured current boot: kernel 13.274 s; userspace 25.194 s. Sable service
+started at monotonic 49.85 s; Volumio connected at 56.55 s. The clock gate
+expired at 177.09 s, only then starting rotary, IR and buttons.
+
+Changes:
+- Player connectivity now releases normal Sable startup independently of NTP.
+- NTP checking continues on a daemon thread. The idle screen says Ready to play
+  until time is trusted, rather than displaying a potentially wrong clock.
+- Audio CD maps to assets/menu/audio_cd.png, a distinct disc glyph.
+- A Rip CD row appears only when Volumio advertises the CD rip action.
+- Rip CD requests getRipInfo; cdRipStart supplies metadata and destinations.
+  Selecting Rip to Internal Memory submits ripCD with the complete returned
+  metadata and destinationDrive, matching the installed Volumio web client.
+- Cancel, absent destinations, disabled ripping, send failures and option
+  timeouts are handled. Backend notifications appear on the rip status frame;
+  detailed progress remains in Volumio.
+- AGENTS.md records .19 as the persistent project default.
+- Corrected an existing joined Restart/RestartSec line in the service SOURCE.
+  The installed /etc service was not edited or reloaded in this update.
+
+Validation: 8 new CD/boot tests, 6 home tests, 8 browse tests, 1 splash test
+passed; changed Python modules compile; ascii_guard passed. Carousel preview:
+previews/audio-cd.png. Rip API and destination were read from the live Pi;
+no actual rip was started and playback was left alone. No restart or reboot
+was issued. New cold-boot timing and a complete rip remain to be verified.
+
+Pre-edit file backups: backups/2026-10-02-cd-boot-225058/.
diff --git a/docs/2026-10-02-cd-recovery.md b/docs/2026-10-02-cd-recovery.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a2798f8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/2026-10-02-cd-recovery.md
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# CD menu recovery and two ripping formats
+
+User requested restoring the clock gate after the faster startup felt unreliable.
+Full startup again requires clock sync AND player connectivity, bounded by the
+existing display.boot_gate_s (120 seconds). The time checker stays off-thread.
+
+CD menu loading was not reproducible in a fresh connected client, but live logs
+showed player reconnects. Pending navigation is now resent on reconnect; explicit
+navigation cancels an outstanding shortcut collection and filters mismatched
+reply URIs. Loading gets 25 seconds without the old 10-second menu expiry,
+then shows Retry and Back. A successful reply gives a fresh navigation interval.
+
+Live home-to-CD integration test: 21 rows loaded from the inserted R.E.M. CD,
+starting with Play all, Rip HQ, Rip MP3 and the tracks. Preview:
+previews/cd-rip-menu.png.
+
+Rip HQ = original-resolution lossless FLAC. Rip MP3 = 320 kbps MP3.
+Volumio supplies CD metadata and available storage. Sable uses the already
+installed cdparanoia and ffmpeg to rip sequentially; it does not modify
+Volumio's protected CD plugin or global abcde config. Files go under:
+<selected drive>/CD Rips/<artist>/<album> - HQ or MP3 <unique suffix>/.
+Tags include artist, album, title, track number and year when supplied.
+Destination/disc identity/free space are checked. Existing files are not
+replaced; concurrent Sable/abcde rips are rejected. CD playback is stopped only
+when a rip begins. New files trigger Volumio's updateDb command on completion.
+Progress can be reopened by selecting a rip option while a job is running.
+Power interruption stops a job; completed tracks remain, with no auto-resume.
+
+Tests cover menu/reconnect/timeout/clock logic, navigation, real ffmpeg encoding
+on synthetic PCM (FLAC decoded bytes equal the original; MP3 verified 320 kbps),
+and changed-disc rejection. No actual disc was ripped and no service restarted.
+Hardware menu behaviour, complete physical CD ripping and next boot remain
+user/live checks after reboot. Previous backup:
+backups/2026-10-02-cd-recovery-231517/.
diff --git a/docs/2026-10-02-clock-storage.md b/docs/2026-10-02-clock-storage.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c106a7e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/2026-10-02-clock-storage.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Clock display and destination corrections
+
+Restored the original ClockScreen even after the bounded boot clock timeout.
+The Ready to play / Clock syncing replacement screen is removed.
+The boot gate still waits for time AND player connectivity, or its timeout.
+
+ntpsec stepped the clock at 23:28:39 but Sable only recognized synchronization
+at 23:34:01. Instead of rejecting leap_alarm unconditionally, the clock checker
+can now confirm three distinct fresh peer samples (<=90 sec old), all within
+128 ms of local time and agreeing within 50 ms. Stale, unreachable, invalid,
+noisy and obviously incorrect samples are rejected. Stratum alone is not used.
+
+ntpsec already uses iburst and -g -N, but /var/lib/ntpsec/ntp.drift was absent.
+Saved its measured frequency -14.644592 ppm when the selected peer existed and
+offset was -2.004 ms, owned ntpsec:ntpsec, for next-start calibration. Existing
+daemon configuration and running process were not changed. Startup improvement
+still requires measurement at next boot. NTPsec reference:
+https://docs.ntpsec.org/latest/ntpd.html#_starting_ntp_best_current_practice
+
+The ripping destination check incorrectly rejected /mnt/INTERNAL because it
+resolves to /data/INTERNAL. USB similarly resolves from /mnt/USB to /media.
+Both allowed roots are now resolved before comparison. A selected USB disk must
+still be a live mount. Library refresh uses the logical INTERNAL/CD Rips or
+USB/<disk>/CD Rips path, not its physical storage path.
+
+Verified Samba's Internal Storage share points at /data/INTERNAL, and performed
+a temporary write/readability check in the real CD Rips folder (test file removed
+by its context manager). Live clock check returns true. Three clock/storage
+regression tests, 13 CD/boot tests and three rip/encoding tests passed.
+No physical CD was ripped, and no service restart or reboot was issued.
+USB choice comes from Volumio's availableDrives; no USB pen was present to test.
diff --git a/docs/2026-10-02-rip-options.md b/docs/2026-10-02-rip-options.md
