index 0000000..2442847
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/2026-10-02-rip-options.md
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Rip options timeout: diagnosed and corrected
+
+Volumio journal during user failures showed getRipInfo invoking abcde -a cddb,
+which failed with missing oggenc and EISDIR reading the CDDB file. Consequently
+no cdRipStart reply reached Sable. Merely increasing the timeout would not fix it.
+
+Sable now caches the CD navigation metadata it actually displayed, reads the
+current disc TOC with cd-discid, validates the track count and lists internal
+storage plus mounted USB disks directly. This runs on a background thread;
+no getRipInfo call or abcde/oggenc is involved. The existing ripping worker
+still validates disc identity again before reading tracks. No external CD
+plugin or packages were modified. Unavailable drives and read errors report
+clear messages; timeout/error screens no longer say Keep Pi powered on.
+
+Both HQ and MP3 destination menus were tested end-to-end against the real
+inserted CD without selecting the destination or initiating a rip. Twenty
+regression checks passed across CD/boot, encoding and clock/storage tests.
+No service restart or reboot issued. A full physical rip still needs a live run.
