+# Ripped album visibility
+
+The unique album directory created with tempfile.mkdtemp inherited mode 0700.
+MPD runs as mpd, so it could list the artist parent but not the album contents.
+Set new album directories to 0755 and finished songs to 0644. Temporary track
+folders remain private. Corrected the completed R.E.M. album and requested a
+scoped Volumio updateDb. API browse now returns the album and its 17 tracks.
+All five worker tests pass, including output permissions for FLAC and MP3.
diff --git a/docs/2026-10-03-rip-progress.md b/docs/2026-10-03-rip-progress.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..16b8950
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/2026-10-03-rip-progress.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# CD rip progress and controls
+
+Progress stays visible and awake until the rip finishes or the user exits.
+The bar measures the current track: reading fills the first half from WAV
+bytes against the disc TOC; encoding fills the second half from ffmpeg
+reported audio time. It resets each track. The separate counter remains 4/17.
+Cancel terminates the current reader/encoder, removes temporary track files,
+and retains completed songs. Exit and continue closes the progress screen
+without stopping the background rip. Existing music is never overwritten.
+
+Validation: 18 CD/boot checks and 5 worker checks passed, including real
+FLAC lossless sample verification, real 320kbps MP3 encoding, subprocess
+cancellation, measured progress, track reset, screen timeout and idle guards.
+Rendered preview: docs/previews/cd-rip-progress.png.
+
+Files are saved on .19. No restart or reboot was performed; the existing
+rip was left running. Changes take effect after the next Sable start.
