 Description=Sable Display (Quadify successor) - OLED + rotary + spectrum
 # Sable's display app owns SPI (SSD1322) and the rotary GPIO. It must NOT run
 # alongside quadify.service (which owns the same SPI/GPIO) -- the installer
-# disables quadify.service + cava.service, plus the legacy quadify-buttonsleds
-# and ir_listener services (see install.sh's retirement loop). Buttons, LEDs,
-# and IR are NOT separate services in this deployment -- this single process
-# (--stage full) owns all of them in-process (see inputs/buttons.py,
-# inputs/ir.py). controls.py + the sable-controls/-display/-ir/-moode systemd
-# templates describe an alternate split-process architecture that is not the
-# one this unit runs; verified live 2026-08-19 (only sable.service running).
-After=network.target volumio.service sable-boot-splash.service
-Wants=volumio.service
+# disables quadify.service + cava.service. Buttons/LEDs (quadify-buttonsleds)
+# and IR (ir_listener) are independent services and keep running.
